A block with a mapping widget (a listing, an RSS feed, search shortcuts, related items) always stores its `fieldMapping`, and every entry is `{ field, type }`, carrying its conversion: the listing is expanded where there is no schema to work one out. `expandListingBlocks` has no default mapping any more: it refuses a listing with no stored mapping, or an entry without a conversion, naming it, rather than passing values through (which put a bare string in a link field, or a list in a title). Picking the item type stores the widget's default for it; the editor refuses to save a block whose mapping is missing or doesn't fit, and the content check reports it. Migrate stored content with `plone-content field-mappings <content-dir> --schemas <schemas>`: it stores the item type's default where there is none, gives every entry its conversion and renames `@id` to `getURL`. A block config's `fieldMappings` may still leave `type` out, since they are read with the schema.
